  "derived_judgments": [
    "Sharing the authoritative compiler is insufficient when its evaluation policy remains batch-shaped; semantic reuse and interactive evaluation policy are distinct architectural concerns.",
    "A separate live engine is justified when it unlocks an end-to-end partial/cancellable/incremental interaction model materially earlier or more reliably than refactoring the authoritative batch engine.",
    "The cost is semantic divergence, so authority must be explicit and common semantic logic or checkable artifacts should be shared where feasible.",
    "For Anneal, the strongest analogy is a live advisory path over revisioned partial state plus an authoritative acceptance path over immutable identified inputs, conditional on the batch path not already meeting live requirements."
  ]
